# Changelog

### Added
- Connect timeout for all connections to Microsoft (`http.connect_timeout`, default 1 second). It only limits
  DNS resolution, TCP connect and TLS handshake, running transfers are not affected.
  - Graph API requests: `TimeoutAwareGraph`, `TimeoutAwareGraphRequest` and `TimeoutAwareGraphCollectionRequest`
    create their Guzzle clients via `GuzzleClientFactory`, which adds `connect_timeout` to the Graph SDK settings.
  - Symfony HttpClient (token, chunk upload, download): `ConnectTimeoutHttpClient` decorator, service
    `perspeqtive.flysystem_one_drive.http_client`.
- Configurable total timeout of Graph API requests (`http.request_timeout`, default 100 seconds as in the Graph SDK).
- Path based site lookup via the optional drive config `site: { hostname, path }`, which avoids the slow
  `/sites?search=` endpoint. Drives without `site` (or with `site: ~`) keep using the search. The `path` may be
  decoded or percent-encoded.
- `SiteIdResolverInterface` (service `perspeqtive.flysystem_one_drive.site.site_id_resolver`) to resolve the site id
  of a configured drive, resolved ids are cached per service instance.
- `GraphFactoryInterface`, `TokenProviderInterface`, `SiteNotFoundException`, `UnknownDriveException`,
  `ConnectTimeoutException`.

### Changed
- The `options` of a drive are now passed to the `OneDriveAdapter` (`directory_type` is always `sites`).
  An invalid `chunk_size` (not a multiple of 327680) now throws when the adapter is created.
- The credentials are no longer merged into the drive options.
- `GraphProvider` requires a `GraphFactoryInterface` and depends on `TokenProviderInterface`.
  `refreshGraphToken()` creates the Graph instance if it does not exist yet instead of failing.
- `OneDriveFlysystemFactory` requires a `SiteIdResolverInterface` and throws `UnknownDriveException`.
- Service definitions moved from `config/services.xml` to `config/services.yaml` (XML is deprecated in Symfony 7.4).
- `FlysystemOneDriveAdapterBundle`, `GraphProvider`, `TokenProvider` and `OneDriveFlysystemFactory` are final.
- `TimeoutAwareGraphCollectionRequest::count()` throws a `GraphException` instead of triggering a notice when the
  count is unavailable.
